title: Party Finances
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and dues_timer <= 0
on-arrival: dues_timer = 4; month_actions += 1
frequency: 300
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs

= Party Finances

A revolutionary party still has to pay for paper, printing presses, offices and train tickets. The district treasurers are waiting to hear what the Zentrale expects of them.

[? if inflation >= 60 : The mark is falling by the day. Dues collected on Friday are worth half as much by the time they reach Berlin. ?][? if inflation < 60 and year >= 1921 : The party is far bigger than it was, but most of its members are poor, and many are out of work. ?]

- @maintain: Collect the usual dues.
- @raise: Ask the members for more.
- @lower: Cut dues for the unemployed.
- @stable: Fix the dues in stable money.
- @easy_discard

@maintain
subtitle: [? if inflation < 80 : [+ dues +] funds gained. ?][? if inflation >= 80 : One fund gained: the rest is eaten by inflation. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += (Q.inflation >= 80) ? 1 : Q.dues;
!}

The district treasurers send in what they have.

@raise
subtitle: [+ dues + 1 +] funds gained. Members are poor, and some will drift away.
view-if: inflation < 80
choose-if: dues < 4
unavailable-subtitle: The members cannot pay any more than they do.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dues += 1;
Q.resources += Q.dues;
Q.worker_support -= 2;
Q.unity -= 2;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.98;
}
!}

The money comes in, with complaints. In a hungry year, every pfennig counts.

@lower
subtitle: No funds this month, and less from now on. The unemployed stay in the party, and more join.
choose-if: dues >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Dues are already as low as they can go.
on-arrival: {!
Q.dues -= 1;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 1.04;
}
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 2;
!}

The party card stays in the pocket of the man on the dole. He will remember who kept it there.

@stable
subtitle: [+ dues +] funds gained, whatever the mark does. The poorest members cannot keep up.
view-if: inflation >= 60
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += Q.dues;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_members'] *= 0.97;
}
Q.unity -= 2;
!}

Dues are now reckoned in gold marks and collected on payday, before the money loses its value. The treasurers keep their accounts in dollars and rye.
